---
name: Multi-month KPI score inheritance and re-percolation
description: Terminal month auto-percolates scores to siblings on approval AND on post-approval edits; siblings are placeholders
type: feature
---
For multi-month KPIs (Bi-Monthly, Quarterly, Half-Yearly, Yearly), only the chronologically terminal month of each cycle goes through the workflow. Sibling months are placeholders.

When the terminal month transitions to `approved`, the `percolate_multimonth_score` trigger force-copies the full submission snapshot (all stage scores, ratings, achieved values, remarks, evidence) to every sibling AND sets `kpis.status = 'approved'`, regardless of the sibling's prior stage. The trigger sets `app.percolation_bypass = 'true'` (transaction-local) so the existing `enforce_frequency_lock_on_submission` trigger does not block its own legitimate writes.

**Post-approval re-percolation** (§54 v4): If scores on the terminal month's `review_submissions` row are modified after approval, `trg_repercolate_on_submission_update` (AFTER UPDATE on `review_submissions`) automatically propagates updated scores to sibling submissions. Uses `app.repercolation_active = 'true'` as recursion guard. Audit action: `SCORE_REPERCOLATED` with `metadata.policy = 'POLICY_54_v4'`.

**Cycle terminal resolution**: use `get_cycle_months(frequency, period, year, frequency_cycle_start)`. The terminal month is the highest calendar index in the array, EXCEPT when the cycle wraps Dec→Jan, in which case trust the array's last element. Client-side mirror: `getActiveMonthForCycle()` in `src/lib/frequencyUtils.ts`.

**Guards**:
- Trigger only fires when `NEW.review_period == terminal_month`. Approving an earlier month (e.g. Feb in a Feb-Mar cycle) MUST NOT overwrite the later one.
- `workflow_change_step_back` skips non-terminal siblings — scores follow the terminal, not the local workflow.
- Non-Admin UI submissions on siblings are blocked by `enforce_frequency_lock_on_submission`. Admins bypass via the existing has_role check.

**Forbidden**:
- Do NOT re-introduce a sibling-stage guard or `PERCOLATION_DEFERRED` audit action inside `percolate_multimonth_score` — that was the bug fixed on 2026-04-29.
- Do NOT call `UPDATE kpis SET status = …` on a sibling from a SECURITY DEFINER context without first `PERFORM set_config('app.percolation_bypass','true',true)`.

**Audit actions**:
- `SCORE_PERCOLATED` (metadata.policy = 'POLICY_54_v3', forced=true) — runtime trigger
- `SCORE_REPERCOLATED` (metadata.policy = 'POLICY_54_v4') — post-approval re-percolation trigger
- `BACKFILL_MULTIMONTH_PERCOLATION` (performed_by = NULL) — one-shot historical repair on 2026-04-29 (142 terminals → 23 siblings)

See POLICY.md §54 v3/v4 and ADR-047.

**Sibling creation at assignment time** (2026-05-07): `useCreateKpi` now expands multi-month assignments by inserting placeholder sibling rows (`status='kra_set'`) for every cycle month from the admin-selected `Effective Month` forward, excluding past months and locked periods (filtered via `review_period_locks` + `review_periods.is_locked`). The terminal row is still inserted first as the workflow target. Helper: `src/lib/multimonthAssignment.ts::buildSiblingPeriods`. This makes the KPI visible to employees in every open cycle month and lets monthly weighted scores treat it as "pending" rather than "missing" until the terminal is approved.
